# TypeScript / React Coding Standards

Canonical narrative: **`docs/typescript_coding_standards.md`**. ESLint rule set: **`eslint.config.js`**. Companion feed server standards live in [dp1-feed-v2 **`docs/go_coding_standards.md`**](https://github.com/display-protocol/dp1-feed-v2/blob/main/docs/go_coding_standards.md) for cross-repo context only.

## 1) Readability first

- Prefer straightforward types and narrow functions over abstraction for its own sake.
- Components stay focused on UI flow; extract helpers when JSX becomes a logic swamp.
- Name hooks **`use*`**; use **`camelCase`** for values/functions and **`PascalCase`** for components exported as React views.

## 2) Errors and boundaries

- Use **`FeedAPIError`** from `src/lib/api.ts` (or successors) so HTTP failures carry **status** and stable **`error`** when the feed returns it.
- Do not silently swallow failures; surface user-visible or developer-actionable diagnostics.
- Parse unknown JSON explicitly at boundaries; avoid widening types without reason.

## 3) Modules and layering

- **HTTP:** `src/lib/api.ts`
- **Signing / JCS / EIP-191:** `src/lib/signing.ts` and related payload helpers
- **Types:** `src/types/`
- Avoid embedding fetch/signing deep inside unrelated presentational helpers.

## 4) React-specific

- Prefer controlled forms and deliberate refetch/state keys when swapping entities (avoid stale PATCH merges).
- Context providers expose narrow APIs; misuse should fail fast (`useDp1Extensions`).

## 5) Testing

- When a test runner is added, prioritize pure helpers (URI validation, merge, canonical signing inputs) over snapshotting large trees.
- Until then: **`npm run build`** exercises `tsc`; keep it green.

## 6) Verification

- **`npm run lint`** must pass (`eslint.config.js`).
- **`npm run build`** must pass for changes that touch TypeScript.
